     mmkkffiiffoo — make FIFOs

SSYYNNOOPPSSIISS
     mmkkffiiffoo [--mm _m_o_d_e] _f_i_f_o___n_a_m_e _._._.

DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
     mmkkffiiffoo creates the FIFOs requested, in the order specified, using mode
     0666 modified by the current umask(2).  It requires write permission in
     the parent directory.

     The options are as follows:

     --mm _m_o_d_e
             Set the file permission bits of newly created FIFOs to _m_o_d_e.  The
             mode argument can be in any of the formats specified to the
             chmod(1) utility.  If a symbolic mode is specified, the operators
             ‘+’ and ‘-’ are interpreted relative to an initial mode of
             “a=rw”.

EEXXIITT SSTTAATTUUSS
     The mmkkffiiffoo utility exits 0 on success, and >0 if an error occurs.

SSEEEE AALLSSOO
     mkdir(1), rm(1), mkfifo(2), mknod(8)

SSTTAANNDDAARRDDSS
     The mmkkffiiffoo utility is compliant with the IEEE Std 1003.1-2008 (“POSIX.1”)
     specification.

HHIISSTTOORRYY
     The mmkkffiiffoo command appeared in 4.3BSD-Reno.

